---
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/legal-page.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "purpose", title: "Purpose & Core Principles" },
  { id: "scope", title: "Scope & Applicability" },
  { id: "expected-behavior", title: "Expected Behavior" },
  { id: "unacceptable-behavior", title: "Unacceptable Behavior" },
  { id: "exhibitors-sponsors", title: "Exhibitors & Sponsors" },
  { id: "reporting", title: "Reporting an Incident" },
  { id: "enforcement", title: "Enforcement & Penalties" },
  { id: "license", title: "License & Attribution" },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Code of Conduct"
  subtitle="Our commitment to providing a safe, respectful, and inclusive conference experience for everyone in the Indonesian software developer community."
  toc={toc}
  currentPath="/code-of-conduct">
  <!-- Key takeaway callout box -->
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/60 p-5 text-sm text-blue-950">
    <p class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-1">Guiding Principle</p>
    <p class="text-blue-900/90 leading-relaxed">
      All participants—including in-person and online attendees, speakers, sponsors, exhibitors, volunteers, and
      staff—must abide by this Code of Conduct. The safety and comfort of all participants take precedence above all
      else.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: Purpose -->
  <section id="purpose" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      1. Purpose & Core Principles
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Indonesia Software Developer Conference (IDSW 2026), organized by Perkumpulan Pengrajin Kode Indonesia (PERKODI),
      is dedicated to fostering an open, collaborative, and harassment-free community conference.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We believe that the developer ecosystem thrives when diverse perspectives are welcomed with mutual respect and
      professionalism. Every individual deserves an enjoyable, productive, and safe conference experience, regardless of
      their background, identity, or level of technical experience.
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-3 pt-2 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Respect Everyone</span>
        Treat all participants with professional courtesy, empathy, and dignity.
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Zero Tolerance</span>
        Discrimination or harassment in any form is strictly prohibited.
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Safety First</span>
        Follow instructions from event staff. Participant safety and comfort come first.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Scope -->
  <section id="scope" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      2. Scope & Applicability
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      This Code of Conduct applies to all participants across all event contexts and touchpoints:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>In-Person Venue:</strong> Usmar Ismail Hall, Jakarta, including auditorium stages, exhibition areas, hallways,
        networking lounges, restrooms, and associated venue facilities.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Online Channels:</strong> Official livestream chats, social media channels, and community groups.
        <li>
          <strong>Official & Unofficial Associated Gatherings:</strong> Speaker dinners, pre-conference mixers, after-parties,
          and community meetups bearing the IDSW name or partnership.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>All Roles:</strong> Attendees, speakers, sponsors, booth staff, organizers, volunteers, and media partners.
        </li>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Section 3: Expected Behavior -->
    <section id="expected-behavior" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        3. Expected Behavior
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        We expect all participants to uphold the following standards:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Practice inclusive and respectful communication:</strong> Use welcoming language, listen constructively,
          and value differing professional viewpoints.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Follow staff instructions:</strong> Comply promptly with directions given by IDSW organizers, venue management,
          and security personnel.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Respect shared spaces and personal boundaries:</strong> Be mindful of physical space, personal comfort,
          and accessibility needs of fellow attendees.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Be attentive to fellow participants:</strong> If you see someone in distress, experiencing discomfort, or
          facing inappropriate behavior, offer assistance or alert event staff immediately.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Professional conduct:</strong> Introduce yourself courteously. Solicitation, product pitches, or promotional
          activities must be respectful and consensual.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Unacceptable Behavior -->
    <section id="unacceptable-behavior" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        4. Unacceptable Behavior
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        Harassment and discriminatory conduct will not be tolerated under any circumstances. Unacceptable behaviors
        include, but are not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
        <li>
          Offensive verbal or written comments related to gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability,
          physical appearance, body size, race, ethnicity, age, or religion.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use of sexualized images, language, jokes, or provocative material in presentations, slides, or public spaces.
        </li>
        <li>
          Deliberate intimidation, stalking, following, or harassing photography and video recording without consent.
        </li>
        <li>Sustained disruption of presentations, workshops, panel discussions, or networking sessions.</li>
        <li>Inappropriate physical contact or unwelcome sexual attention of any nature.</li>
        <li>
          Aggressive commercial solicitation, unsolicited direct promotional spamming, or disruptive guerrilla marketing
          without prior sponsor authorization.
        </li>
        <li>Advocating for, or encouraging, any of the above behaviors.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 bg-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-3">
        <strong>Immediate Compliance:</strong> Participants asked by staff, speakers, or attendees to stop any harassing or
        disruptive behavior are required to comply immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Exhibitors & Sponsors -->
    <section id="exhibitors-sponsors" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        5. Exhibitors & Sponsors
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        Exhibitors in sponsor booths, partner lounges, and demo areas are fully subject to this anti-harassment policy:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
        <li>
          Exhibitors and booth staff (including hired promoters and volunteers) must not use sexualized imagery,
          costumes, or activities.
        </li>
        <li>
          Promotional activities, giveaways, and booth games must maintain a professional and welcoming atmosphere for
          all conference attendees.
        </li>
        <li>Staff must respect participants' decision to engage or walk away from marketing conversations.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: Reporting an Incident -->
    <section id="reporting" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        6. Reporting an Incident
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        If you experience harassment, observe that someone else is being harassed, or have any other safety or comfort
        concerns, please notify the organizers immediately through either of the following channels:
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 pt-1">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 text-sm mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-primary" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z"></path>
            </svg>
            In-Person at the Venue
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            Approach any member of the IDSW organizing committee or volunteer crew on duty at Usmar Ismail Hall. Staff
            can be easily identified by official <strong>IDSW staff badges, shirts, or crew passes</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 text-sm mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-primary" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z"
              ></path>
            </svg>
            Email Reporting
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
            Send an email to <a
              href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org?subject=Reporting%20Code%20of%20Conduct%20Violation"
              class="text-primary font-semibold underline">idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
            > with the subject line <em>"Reporting Code of Conduct Violation"</em> for prioritized monitoring and immediate
            response.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        Event staff are prepared to help participants contact hotel and venue security or local Indonesian law
        enforcement, provide safe escorts, or otherwise assist those experiencing harassment to feel secure for the
        entire duration of the conference.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 7: Enforcement & Penalties -->
    <section id="enforcement" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        7. Enforcement & Penalties
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        The IDSW Organizing Committee and PERKODI reserve the right to take appropriate disciplinary actions against
        anyone who violates this Code of Conduct, including but not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
        <li>Issuing a formal verbal or written reprimand.</li>
        <li>Immediate expulsion from the conference without refund or reimbursement.</li>
        <li>Permanent ban from attending or speaking at future IDSW and PERKODI-affiliated events.</li>
        <li>Reporting criminal conduct to venue management and local law enforcement authorities.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 8: License & Attribution -->
    <section id="license" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
        8. License & Attribution
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        This Code of Conduct is adapted from the PyCon US and PyCon ID Code of Conduct policies and is licensed under
        the
        <a
          href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-primary underline">
          Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported License
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
